    "text": "But chips are not tanks. They're smaller than a fingernail. Many cost just a few dollars. And billions of them are sold every year through thousands of distributors around the world. The chip that guides a missile can be the very same chip that runs a car, a drone or a washing machine. Once it leaves the factory, it can be sold again and again and again. And every time it changes hands, it gets harder to know where it ends up.",
